":"35a6fb919e64e4fa9ae1f0bf0f6648b5530acb4be3bfcba30edb417e0c1f9329","event_uuid":"4ffea8d8-0c62-435b-ada5-3742e9b29139","position":{"commit_sha":"a134b8dbbbc3bd409a97da1065e2c8fd298c7bc3","position":"1787560089777066001-4ffea8d8-0c62-435b-ada5-3742e9b29139"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"7f40c619f4feabb81b6d28059bc50c37fc5ed584ab0ba1c3383363ea2eee6095","event_uuid":"5973e9da-373e-4b24-adb1-dfc78b8b6f61","position":{"commit_sha":"fee78038ccd1718049c629e8aa05316be07c1bea","position":"1787560742518597001-5973e9da-373e-4b24-adb1-dfc78b8b6f61"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"86eb92568d7a39e3c66b521d5c228f5ced91f2e205c4bd8c7e5a0b1c415e784f","event_uuid":"dc622656-981a-4a2d-97fc-aa252650fdb8","position":{"commit_sha":"8ea34199393c4794e68080bd95429416537c4e1a","position":"1787560765723349001-dc622656-981a-4a2d-97fc-aa252650fdb8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"a9b1e62ba00f7909b8c4d98980e2105e7af1ea6c07f9855fe1debb38d50d28e4","event_uuid":"45dbdf91-00f0-49c1-8fe9-d3beb6aef225","position":{"commit_sha":"40a38b5993e131c1ec4a6acaed95d3b8c137307f","position":"1787560806767789001-45dbdf91-00f0-49c1-8fe9-d3beb6aef225"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"0858009544a90cb6aaab3345e8d62fb204a5796c95b7f230e060c551ff14d995","event_uuid":"edadd17c-431e-494f-b01f-1f7285a14be9","position":{"commit_sha":"cd5782854c473f2b48c168e841467e236f8921a8","position":"1787560914996130001-edadd17c-431e-494f-b01f-1f7285a14be9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"rebar-debug Phase 1 RCA (confirmed at runtime).\n\nMechanism: impact-present close -> close_precheck._check_work_landed -> commit_impact.referencing_commits, which walks all code history and resolves every extracted historical candidate via resolve_ticket_id. The prior alias-index fix (commit 5c64deff, ticket 4234-821b) bounded ONLY the alias branch: build_alias_index runs one store pass and resolve_ticket_id(alias_index=...) does an in-memory lookup for aliases. The RESIDUAL is the two other resolution branches in src/rebar/_ids.py:resolve_ticket_id that still call os.listdir(tracker_dir) once PER candidate:\n - the 8-hex short-id branch (_SHORT_ID_RE; matches[...] over os.listdir when no exact dir), and\n - the generic prefix branch (len>=4; n.startswith(ticket_id) over os.listdir).\nOrdinary subject prefixes, deprecated 4-digit fragments, and short-id-shaped tokens that name no dir all fall through the alias_index (which returns [] for a non-alias) into these two branches, so each unique historical candidate drives a fresh full tracker-root listing -> O(unique_candidates x tracker) directory listings before completion verification. This is the impact-present 'history x tracker' scaling the ticket names.\n\nRuntime proof: a synthetic repo with a target credited by alias plus 80 distinct non-alias candidate trailers (40 short-id-shaped, 40 four-digit) recorded 82 tracker-root os.listdir scans during referencing_commits (1 index build + one per candidate), target still correctly credited. Falsifiable prediction held: had only the alias path been the cost, scans would be <=1; instead they scaled linearly with candidates.\n\nRivals rejected: (a) 'alias-index already fixed it' — refuted, aliases ARE bounded but short-id/prefix are not; (b) 'os.listdir is negligible' — it is a full tracker-root listing (5.3k entries) per candidate, i.e. exactly the walk AC#1 forbids and the mechanism the pre-5c64deff 25-62m telemetry sampled (the alias JSON-read cost has since been removed, leaving this listing cost).\n\nLegitimacy: defect. AC#1/#2 require bounded work; the current short-id/prefix branches perform a full tracker walk per candidate.\n\nOrigin: the impact-present close landing scan that resolves arbitrary historical candidates was introduced by 746c1ba2e961 'Add attach-commits verb and impact-vs-diff gate' (ticket cec6-0a0e-38a9-4234); the alias sub-case was later partially bounded by 4234-821b, leaving the short-id/prefix residual. Phase 2 (RED-first) unlocked.","timestamp":1787552009347647001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"rebar-debug Phase 2 repair report.\n\nProblem: impact-present ticket close ran commit_impact.referencing_commits, whose per-candidate historical-reference resolution still performed a full tracker-root os.listdir for every 8-hex short-id and generic-prefix/four-digit candidate (the alias branch was already bounded by 5c64deff). O(unique_candidates x tracker).\n\nRoot cause (proven): resolve_ticket_id's _SHORT_ID_RE branch and its len>=4 generic-prefix branch each called os.listdir(tracker_dir) per candidate. Non-alias candidates fall through the alias index (which returns [] for a non-alias) straight into these two branches.\n\nRED-first test: tests/unit/test_attach_commits.py::test_referencing_commits_bounded_scans_for_non_alias_candidates counts tracker-root os.listdir calls during referencing_commits with 50 distinct non-alias candidate trailers (25 short-id-shaped + 25 four-digit) plus an alias-credited target. It failed RED at 52 scans (<=1 required) and is GREEN after the fix. The target commit stays correctly credited.\n\nFix: added build_resolver_scan_index (one tracker-root pass -> ResolverScanIndex{alias_to_dirs, sorted_dir_names}). resolve_ticket_id gained an optional dir_names= param; the short-id and generic-prefix branches were extracted into _resolve_short_id/_resolve_prefix, which prefix-match the prebuilt sorted dir-name list by bisect (O(log store + matches)) when the index is supplied and otherwise keep the exact per-call os.listdir behavior. referencing_commits now builds the combined index once and threads both alias_index= and dir_names=. build_alias_index is retained as the alias-only view. No semantics changed: same match set, same ambiguity handling, same fail-closed None-vs-[] contract, descendant credit / --ref / file-impact-vs-diff untouched.\n\nBefore/after evidence (synthetic large-history repro, 80 distinct non-alias candidates + 1 alias-credited target):\n - before: 82 tracker-root os.listdir scans (1 index build + 80 per-candidate + verify wrap), scaling linearly with candidates.\n - after: 1 tracker-root scan (the single index build), target still credited.\nBounded to one tracker index/build per invocation plus linear code-history parsing, satisfying AC#1/#2/#6.\n\nParity: tests/unit/test_attach_commits.py::test_indexed_short_id_and_prefix_resolution_matches_per_call proves indexed short-id, unique/ambiguous generic-prefix, and longer-prefix resolution equal per-call scanning (None on ambiguity), pinning AC#3 for the newly indexed branches. Existing alias parity/perf tests remain green.\n\nGates: complexity baseline --check active=42 new=0 increased=0 (resolve_ticket_id dropped below its ceiling -> stale, the sanctioned improvement; baseline left untouched); make lint and make typecheck (mypy 645 files) clean; 772 resolver/close-related unit tests + 26 attach/alias-perf tests pass. Module sizes: _ids.py 496 LOC, commit_impact.py 218 LOC (< 800 cap).\n\nScope/safety sweep: build_alias_index/resolve_ticket_id have one production index-caller (referencing_commits); single-id callers keep the default dir_names=None (unchanged path). No new dependency or capability; no test weakened.\n\nOrigin (caused_by): 746c1ba2e961 'Add attach-commits verb and impact-vs-diff gate' (ticket cec6-0a0e-38a9-4234) introduced the impact-present landing scan over arbitrary historical candidates; alias sub-case bounded by 4234-821b, this closes the short-id/prefix residual.","timestamp":1787552944620806001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed via Gerrit change 2175 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2175), submitted MERGED to main with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 (CI run 32702486475, all pytest matrix + bounded mutation gate green). Closed class=preexisting, caused_by=cec6-0a0e-38a9-4234. Fix: build the resolver index once (alias map + sorted dir-name list) and resolve short-id/generic-prefix historical candidates by bisect instead of a per-candidate os.listdir; before/after 82 -> 1 tracker-root scans for 80 non-alias candidates.","timestamp":1787560914996130001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787525881223169001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"8e014de3-8a95-4fc9-8ce9-d82074110b87","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"4000-2df3-398d-44e2"},{"link_uuid":"4b52bb55-2f6a-43b0-a4e0-1e99004b9cbe","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f380-19d4-4b2f-4bf8"},{"link_uuid":"4c10ee02-9e15-4b56-bbc2-35f3ae915ad1","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6955-e33b-ef40-458c"},{"link_uuid":"378ba376-4b17-46a4-9eaf-2fbc6ae2c0f3","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"dbfa-ddaf-c375-4eed"},{"link_uuid":"45dbdf91-00f0-49c1-8fe9-d3beb6aef225","provenance":"explicit","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"cec6-0a0e-38a9-4234"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe completed fix on reportable-chalkstony-eeve skips full-history commit discovery only when accepted-scope file impact is empty. Impact-present closes still run the same unbounded path, and current end-to-end telemetry shows it now dominates the user-visible close command.\n\nFrozen Codex-rollout sample (2026-08-22 through 2026-08-23T21:15Z), limited to canonical tracker closes with a matched Bedrock COMPLETION_VERDICT and metrics.llm_calls > 0: n=10 completed closes, p50=28.24m, p90=57.32m, p99=61.60m. The matched completion-verifier workflows themselves are generally 1-4m; recent 25-62m closes spend most of their time before the verifier sidecar.\n\nStatic mechanism: close_precheck._check_work_landed calls commit_impact.referencing_commits for every impact-present close. That helper reads all 2,690 commits and extract_ticket_refs produces 2,229 unique historical candidates. 702 candidates require alias/prefix resolution; _scan_alias walks the current 5,351-ticket store for each, implying roughly 3.8 million ticket-directory visits before completion verification. Ordinary subject prefixes and deprecated four-digit references enter the candidate set. This is the residual impact-present case left explicitly unchanged by reportable-chalkstony-eeve.\n\nPost-diagnosis refinement: the alias sub-case was bounded by the sibling fix 4234-821b (commit 5c64deff, one alias-index build). The residual proven at runtime is that resolve_ticket_id's 8-hex short-id branch and its generic >=4-char prefix branch still call os.listdir(tracker_dir) once per candidate, so non-alias candidates (short-id-shaped tokens, ordinary subject prefixes, deprecated four-digit fragments) still scale O(unique_candidates x tracker).\n\n## Plan\n- Add a deterministic performance reproduction for an impact-present close with many historical reference candidates and a large tracker.\n- Replace per-candidate full-store short-id/prefix resolution with a single indexed resolution strategy while preserving every accepted commit-ticket reference form and ambiguity behavior.\n- Keep descendant credit, attached commits, --ref behavior, file-impact-vs-diff enforcement, and fail-closed git-error semantics unchanged.\n- Measure the repaired pre-verifier scan and pin a scaling assertion that prevents history x tracker behavior from returning.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Impact-present close commit discovery does not perform a full tracker walk per unique historical candidate.\n- [x] The scan cost is bounded to one tracker index/build per invocation plus linear code-history parsing.\n- [x] Full, two-quad short, alias, Jira, compatibility four-digit/prefix, trailer, and leading-subject reference forms retain current matching and ambiguity semantics.\n- [x] Descendant ticket credit remains covered end to end.\n- [x] File-impact-vs-diff enforcement remains covered end to end.\n- [x] A scale-focused regression test fails on the current history-times-tracker implementation and passes on the repair.\n- [x] Before/after wall-time and scan-count evidence is recorded on this ticket.\n\n## Testing\n- Verified by `pytest tests/unit/test_attach_commits.py::test_referencing_commits_bounded_scans_for_non_alias_candidates` — RED-first scan-count regression (counts tracker-root `os.listdir` calls; fails on the per-candidate implementation, passes bounded at <=1 on the repair).\n- Verified by `pytest tests/unit/test_attach_commits.py::test_indexed_short_id_and_prefix_resolution_matches_per_call` — indexed short-id / generic-prefix / ambiguous-prefix resolution equals per-call scanning (AC#3).\n- Verified by `pytest tests/unit/test_attach_commits.py -k \"resolver_scan_index or falls_back or work_landed\"` — None-on-hard-failure fail-open contract, per-call fallback crediting, and descendant-credit / file-impact-vs-diff end-to-end checks.\n- Verified by `pytest tests/unit/test_referencing_commits_alias_scan_perf.py` — the alias-branch bound and indexed/per-call parity remain green.\n- Gates: checked with `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check`.\n- Before/after scan-count evidence recorded as a ticket comment (82 -> 1 tracker-root scans for 80 distinct non-alias candidates, target still credited).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/commit_impact.py","reason":"Build the resolver index once and thread alias_index+dir_names into per-candidate resolution for impact-present close discovery."},{"path":"src/rebar/_ids.py","reason":"Add build_resolver_scan_index + sorted dir-name index; resolve short-id/prefix branches via bisect instead of per-candidate os.listdir."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/resolver.py","reason":"Re-export build_resolver_scan_index so the close-precheck scan seam can build the combined index."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_attach_commits.py","reason":"Pin bounded scan-count scaling, indexed/per-call parity, and None-on-hard-failure fallback."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","6955-e33b-ef40-458c"],["relates_to","dbfa-ddaf-c375-4eed"],["relates_to","f380-19d4-4b2f-4bf8"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"5973e9da-373e-4b24-adb1-dfc78b8b6f61","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["performance","completion-gate","discovered"],"ticket_id":"a8ac-48b5-0759-40e5","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Impact-present ticket close scales with code history times tracker size","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["0e7885f8-83c3-4d48-8f28-c0c09e6354da","5806eafc-acd5-474c-a92f-220479dc3ca5","f5acb3f2-193c-4c9e-a19d-0c7ba86ce7e4","19cb22f4-e175-4868-9483-c04d09bfc9a4","4c10ee02-9e15-4b56-bbc2-35f3ae915ad1","aa43d345-345